    {
      "id": "sol.hmmt-feb-guts-2007-p13.hmmt",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "14. We have\n\n\\[7^{2048}-1=(7-1)(7+1)\\left(7^{2}+1\\right)\\left(7^{4}+1\\right) \\cdots\\left(7^{1024}+1\\right)\\]\n\nIn the expansion, the eleven terms other than \\(7+1\\) are divisible by 2 exactly once, as can be checked easily with modulo 4 .",
